.UPDATE...
Issued at 940 AM PDT Wed Jul 29 2026

Water vapor imagery shows a deep trough of lower situated over the
West Coast, with a secondary system moving inland across the
Pacific Northwest. The imagery also shows very dry air aloft
parked over California. Closer to the surface though, the marine
layer deepened slightly overnight in response to the trough, and
pushed farther inland this morning than yesterday. In fact, low
clouds made it all the way inland to Napa and all the way down the
Salinas Valley. That said, the low clouds are starting to
retreat. While the low clouds clear from the inland areas, expect
them to linger once again along the coast today. Otherwise, expect
seasonal and pleasant day across the region, with temperatures
similar to those of yesterday. Forecast is handling these trends
well, so no update is planned at this time. Palmer

