.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 155 PM PDT Tue Jul 28 2026

The elevated fire weather threat will continue across portions of
the area through at least this weekend. Overnight RH recovery
will remain moderate to poor at locations at or above 2,000 feet
with values between 35 to 50 percent, with some favored locations
struggling to even reach 30 percent. This will be particularly
true across the Mayacamas, highest peaks of the East Bay Hills,
the Diablo Range, Santa Cruz Mountains, Santa Lucia and Gabilan
Ranges. Nocturnal drying (rapid decrease in RH through the pre-
dawn hours) may also transpire which will increase the burn period
or time in which fire behavior may remain active. Afternoon RH
will remain critically dry with values between 20 and 40 percent,
with far southern portions of the interior Central Coast
potentially seeing min RH near 10 percent. Energy Release
Components (ERC) are projected to climb above the 95th percentile
across the interior Central Coast. Individuals across the area are
advised to avoid activities that may spark a fire. Fire crews are
urged to exercise extra caution when executing any prescribed
burns, especially where fuels, topography, and weather align.

